        {
          "id": "/page/166/Caption/3",
          "block_type": "Caption",
          "html": "<p></p><p><b>Figure 4.5</b> Geometric illustration of QP. The feasible set <math>\\mathcal{P}</math>, which is a polyhedron, is shown shaded. The contour lines of the objective function, which is convex quadratic, are shown as dashed curves. The point <math>x^*</math> is optimal.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              130.356,
              296.208
            ],
            [
              436.968,
              296.208
            ],
            [
              436.968,
              329.472
            ],
            [
              130.356,
              329.472
            ]
          ],
          "bbox": [
